    "title": "U.K. energy bill proposes changes to waste transport regulation",
    "summary": "A bill introduced in the U.K. Parliament on November 4 includes a provision that potentially would streamline the government’s process for updating rules regarding the transportation of used fuel and radioactive waste. Contained within the Energy Independence Bill are measures that would affect several sectors of the United Kingdom’s energy system in what would amount to a major overhaul. Among the proposals that the legislation calls for are measures to accelerate the deployment of what it identifies as “clean energy” projects, including offshore wind and smart grid projects; support for insulating and otherwise updating residential buildings under the Warm Homes Plan; and an end to licenses for new oil and natural gas exploration.",
